  "scope": "Actual AngelScript Pause screen and real gym shortcut, retained native Settings child, source contracts, input/focus/lifetime scenarios, and compatible authoring checks.",
  "bootPlanDeviation": "The initial combined build/test started inline discovery and a cached worker. Discovery rejected the interaction-owner script binding; the quiet runtime worker exceeded the idle watchdog and respawned. The owned run was cancelled, the binding was repaired and a separate incremental build passed. Gate02 produced no tests: quiet engine material initialization exceeded the idle watchdog, followed by a respawn and renderer fallback. Gate03 restored the successful historical gate's per-run verbose shader logging and completed 14/15 tests. Its sole red assertion incorrectly required both popup Escape press and release to be handled; Slate's menu handler clears focus during dismissal. The fixture was corrected to dispatch both events and assert handled press plus exact popup/child/parent state. Gate04 reruns the same focused population after the incremental fixture build. All logged Editor boots are counted; cancelled attempts provide no runtime verdict.",
  "capabilities": [
    "Actual script class creates UMG shell, imports loose PNG, declares scalars/actions/required buttons and owns source and pause policy.",
    "Real gym [1] creates script Pause; nested native Settings returns to the same script parent/session/view/revision through Cancel and Escape.",
    "Missing/changed required ordinary-button contracts reject before staging; optional empty native configurations remain compatible.",
    "Pure focused-button query supports disable-focused-button navigation repair; EndInput(false) drains and discards saved focus without callbacks.",
    "Interaction-owner config has nullable object-by-value script accessors; actual script round trips null and its derived owner before initialization.",
    "Prepared Settings commits synchronously or expires at next CoreTicker pump without changing retained parent state.",
    "Exact native child push is one-shot; child focus attempts once and has no activation/polling retries.",
    "Script preserves external pause, retires session on terminal clear/removal/layout destroy, and covered parent retains its accepted view.",
    "Exact captured watcher gates terminal removal after child-close callbacks, preserving same-UObject newer admission while releasing old view."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Legacy native Pause functions remain for compatible native screen swaps; Settings/Inventory are not fully migrated and net C++ deletion is not established.",
    "Required title/hint nodes and button label bindings are not declared as mandatory reflected source contracts.",
    "Instant CommonUI transitions only; nonzero transition animation and complete terminal focus reentry are not proved by this fixture.",
    "Prepared-child focus redirection/failure rollback is inspected in production code; this gate does not force that callback path.",
    "Popup Escape is verified to dismiss only the popup; subsequent Cancel is explicitly focused, so automatic focus recovery after dismissal is not proved.",
    "Physical gamepad behavior, packaged lookup, real gameplay persistence/title travel and complete foreign-user action rejection remain unverified.",
    "Second-player lifetime scenarios overlay a single scene view, not two-view split-screen rendering."
  ]
